WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.550
Check yourself with two questions
from the module's knowledge check.

2
00:00:03.550 --> 00:00:07.512
First: what does the code take as
the moment a leaver was blocked?

3
00:00:07.512 --> 00:00:10.332
The answer is b: the
later of the first Disable

4
00:00:10.332 --> 00:00:13.913
account record and the first
session revocation record.

5
00:00:13.913 --> 00:00:16.135
Not the workflow's completion time,

6
00:00:16.135 --> 00:00:20.199
and not the HR effective time,
which is where the interval starts.

7
00:00:20.199 --> 00:00:24.127
Second: a separation is entered
in HR more than three days

8
00:00:24.127 --> 00:00:28.388
after its effective date, and
nobody runs the leaver on demand.

9
00:00:28.388 --> 00:00:30.050
What does the measurement report?

10
00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:32.549
The answer is b: an S T three Finding,

11
00:00:32.549 --> 00:00:37.100
because past three days the
scheduled trigger skips the user.

12
00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:40.087
With an on-demand run,
it would be only a Warn.

13
00:00:40.087 --> 00:00:45.020
The module page has two more questions,
each linked to the section that teaches it.
